@@section 1
@@title SQ-TP Tempad port phase 1: core Tempad, chronons, timedoors, three apps, 2026-11-07 ([immersive_portals.md](../immersive_portals.md) 2.1.1, member notes `development/creativeCompat/members/tempad/PORT_NOTES.md` 9)
@@date 2026-11-07
@@jars creativecompat tempad
@@sources feature_writeup/immersive_portals.md
@@text
@@text Server rows run 2026-11-07 (r1107tp, Run log); without a client they are driven by perfBot bots and `/ztp`
@@text (tools/scratch_query/ztp_probe.js, copy into srv/kubejs/server_scripts). Targets `creativecompat-1.0.0.jar` built 2026-11-07 with `backportedTempad-3.0.4-ce-19.2-01.jar` nested; not in
@@text `mods/` yet. The srv needs `tempad_upstream/tempad-1.21.1-3.0.4-all.jar` (sha1 `7a4d6837...`) next to `mods/`, and no
@@text `tempad-forge-*.jar` in `mods/`. Phase 2-4 work lands later from another session; rerun SQ-TP-01 after each phase.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-TP-01
@group A
@commands boot with the donor present; second boot with `tempad_upstream/` renamed away
@pass first boot reaches `Done (`, no `tempad` errors in latest.log, `/datapack list` shows `tempad_upstream_data`; second boot stops with a message naming `tempad_upstream/` and the jar
@fails translator or pack registration (`forge/UpstreamTranslator`, `BuiltInPacks.addUpstream`); donor sha1 mismatch
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-TP-02 | phase 1 recipes, forge tags, new-location upgrade absent
@group A
@commands `/zq rdetail tempad:tempad`, the same for `chronon_cell`, `chronon_battery`, `chronon_generator`, `chronometer`, `time_steel_shaped`; `/zq rdetail tempad:upgrades/new_location`
@pass each recipe loads with `forge:` tags (ender pearls, quartz, tinted glass); the new-location upgrade recipe is absent while `require_location_upgrade=false`
@fails c: -> forge: tag map in the translator; condition `tempad:required_location_upgrade`
@from batches/r1107tp/a1.qb
> zq rdetail tempad:
waitlog \[zq\] done 60
expect tempad:tempad
expect tempad:chronon_cell
expect tempad:chronon_battery
expect tempad:chronon_generator
expect tempad:chronometer
expect tempad:time_steel_shaped
reject upgrades/new_location
shell grep -hE "\[zq\]" logs/latest.log | grep -E "tempad:(tempad|chronon_cell|chronon_battery|chronon_generator|chronometer|time_steel_shaped) " -A4 | head -60
look inputs use forge: tags (ender pearls, quartz, tinted glass) or items; no c: tags

## SQ-TP-03 | locations and Teleport app after a restart
@group A
@commands `/give` a Tempad and a Creative Chronometer; use the Tempad; save a location with the New Location app; restart; open Teleport
@pass the Teleport app opens; the location is listed after the restart
@fails player capability save / clone (`TempadPlayerData`)
@from batches/r1107tp/a2.qb passed
bootexpect Done \(
> pbot spawn qa 0.5 -60 0.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> ztp locs qa
waitlog \[ztp\] done 20
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Home One" minecraft:overworld 0\.50 -60\.00 0\.50
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Far East" minecraft:overworld 30\.50
expect \[ztp\] loc tempad:default .* "Hell Spot" minecraft:the_nether 0\.50 120\.00
> pbot hold qa tempad:tempad
> zq useitem qa
> ztp menu qa
waitlog \[ztp\] menu 20
expect \[ztp\] menu tempad:teleport

## SQ-TP-04
@group A
@commands Teleport to the saved location in the same dimension and in the Nether; check chronons before and after; use again at once
@pass a timedoor opens, costs 1000 chronons, carries the player; a second door waits for the 40-tick cooldown; the door closes after 200 ticks
@fails `TimedoorEntity`, `forge/Teleports`
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-TP-05 | pinned location + default macro, after restart and after a death
@group A
@commands pin a location, set it as default macro in Settings, shift-use the Tempad; die and respawn, shift-use again
@pass the macro opens a door to the pinned location both times
@fails favourites capability not cloned on respawn
@from batches/r1107tp/a2.qb
> ztp pdata qa
waitlog \[ztp\] pdata 20
expect pinned_location:\{locationId:\[I;-191329597,-100384576,-1821537137,2007787117\],providerId:"tempad:default"\}
> ztp settings qa tempad:teleport tempad:default
> ztp setchr qa 0 6000
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
sleep 3
> ztp macro qa
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
expect \[ztp\] door minecraft:overworld .* target minecraft:overworld \(30\.5, -60\.0, 0\.5\)
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> gamerule keepInventory true
> kill qa
sleep 3
> pbot spawn qa 0.5 -60 0.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> ztp pdata qa
waitlog \[ztp\] pdata 20
count pinned_location:\{locationId:\[I;-191329597 >= 2
> ztp macro qa
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
count \[ztp\] door minecraft:overworld .* target minecraft:overworld \(30\.5, -60\.0, 0\.5\) >= 2
look perfBot relogs a dead bot (no PlayerEvent.Clone): the death half covers save/load only; Clone (copyFrom) needs a client death (CQ note)

## SQ-TP-06 | require_location_upgrade = true
@group A
@commands set `require_location_upgrade = true` in `tempad-common.toml`, restart; open the Tempad without and with the upgrade (craft it into the Tempad)
@pass New Location is missing without the upgrade, present with it; the upgrade item is in the creative tab and has its recipe
@fails ConfigSyncPacket, `ModApps` new-location gate
@from batches/r1107tp/a3.qb
bootexpect Done \(
shell grep -E "require_location_upgrade|cost_per_door|time_in_world" config/tempad-common.toml; grep -A2 "^\[tempad\]" config/tempad-common.toml
> pbot spawn qa 0.5 -60 0.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> clear qa
> item replace entity qa hotbar.0 with tempad:tempad
> ztp apps qa
waitlog \[ztp\] apps 20
expect \[ztp\] apps tempad:settings tempad:teleport$
> item replace entity qa hotbar.0 with tempad:tempad{installed_upgrades:{upgrades:["tempad:new_location"]}}
> ztp apps qa
waitlog \[ztp\] apps tempad:new 20
expect \[ztp\] apps tempad:new_location tempad:settings tempad:teleport
> zq rdetail tempad:upgrades/new_location
waitlog \[zq\] done 30
expect \[zq\] tempad:upgrades/new_location
> zq makes tempad:new_location_upgrade
waitlog \[zq\] done 30
expect \[zq\] .*new_location_upgrade
look upgrade installed by NBT (the crafting of the upgrade into the Tempad is the tempad:upgrade recipe listed here); creative tab is a client check

## SQ-TP-07 | chronon generator charges a carried Tempad
@group A
@commands put a Chronon Generator and a Tempad in the inventory, wait 2 minutes
@pass the Tempad's chronon count rises
@fails chronon capability / generator tick
@from batches/r1107tp/a2.qb
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> clear qa
> give qa tempad:tempad
> give qa tempad:chronon_generator
sleep 1
> ztp chr qa
waitlog \[ztp\] chr end 20
sleep 120
> ztp chr qa
waitlog \[ztp\] chr end 20
shell grep -hE "\[ztp\] chr slot" logs/latest.log | tail -6
look tempad chronons rose between the two chr reads (generator 1 per 48 ticks: about 50 in 2 min)

