@@text
@@text From 2026-11-07 23:01 Tempad is its own jar (`backportedTempad-3.0.4-ce-19.2-01.jar` in `mods/`, no longer nested in `creativecompat-1.0.0.jar`); rows not yet run target that jar. SQ-TP-40 (not run): full pack boots with both jars, `tempad` and `creativecompat` both listed, no duplicate-mod error; Common + Compat alone (no Tempad jar, no `tempad_upstream/`) boots clean (with CQ-CCB-03).
@@text
@@text Not run. Targets `creativecompat-1.0.0.jar` built 2026-11-07 10:31 (`backportedTempad-3.0.4-ce-19.2-01.jar` nested), which
@@text holds the five fixes of TODO #9 plus two found while fixing them (the missing `intradimensional_all` key; array lang
@@text lines that stopped 1.19.2 loading the rest of `tempad_static` lang). Same setup as SQ-TP-01 (donor jar in
@@text `tempad_upstream/`, no `tempad-forge-*.jar`). Rows 21 to 25 / CQ-TP-12 to -14 check the fixes; 26 to 30 / CQ-TP-15 fill the
@@text gaps left by the phase rows above, so SQ-TP-01..30 plus CQ-TP-01..15 cover the whole mod. A FAIL in rows 1 to 20 that
@@text rows 21 to 25 also touch: check it against the fix first (door offsets, messages, momentum, markers, number boxes).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-TP-21
@group A
@commands fix 1: dock a charged Tempad in a Workstation, set offsets x 2, y 1, z -3 in Portal Setup (or on the docked stack's portal-offset NBT), select a location, power it; `/data get entity @e[type=tempad:timedoor,limit=1,sort=nearest] PlacementSettings`; `/save-all`, restart with the power still on, read it again; repeat with the upright toggle off (floor door)
@pass door stands 2 / 1 / -3 off the pad (turned by the pad facing); saved `x`, `y`, `z` are 2, 1, -3, not 1, 1, 1; after the restart the door is in the same place; floor door the same
@fails `FloorPlacementSettings` / `VerticalPlacementSettings` TYPE writer; `WorkstationBE` offset read
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-TP-22
@group A
@commands fixes 2 and 2b: `qrun.py toml` `tempad-common.toml` `allow_intradimensional_travel=false`, restart, Teleport to a same-dimension location; set it back, add a scratch datapack tag `data/tempad/tags/dimension_type/intradimensional_travel_not_supported.json` with `minecraft:overworld`, `/reload`, try again; set `allow_interdimensional_travel=false`, try a Nether location; give the scratch tag file to `leaving_not_supported` and then `entering_not_supported` and try the Nether location each time
@pass no door opens in any of the five cases, chronons unchanged; latest.log has no exception; the message text is checked in CQ-TP-12
@fails `TimedoorEntity.getTimedoor` gates; dimension-type tag folder name on 1.19.2
