## SQ-TP-31
@group A
@commands #10 loot tables load: boot; `grep "Tempad upstream data dropped" logs/debug.log`; `/loot spawn 0 -59 10 loot tempad:blocks/<x>` for workstation, timedoor_marker, chronomark, metronome, timedoor_projector; `kill @e[type=item]`
@pass debug.log names no `loot_table` file (only the NeoForge loot modifier list, the two curios files, advancements); each `/loot spawn` "Dropped 1" of that block; no `Couldn't parse loot table tempad` in latest.log
@fails `UpstreamTranslator.NON_REGISTRY_KEYS` (`random_sequence`); the loot_table -> loot_tables path rename
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-TP-32
@group A
@commands #10 survival drops, bare hand and iron pickaxe: place each of the five blocks (projector and markers with `/ztp sneak qa on` where placing needs shift), give the marker a name (`/ztp markerui`), the chronomark one (`/ztp chronoui`), the metronome a booted pool (`/ztp bchr X Y Z 2000`, wait 6 s), the projector a card and 1500 chronons; `/ztp break qa X Y Z` each, `/ztp pickup qa 24`
@pass exactly one item per block: workstation (plus the docked Tempad when one is docked), marker and chronomark with name, colour, owner and `anchor_id`, metronome with its share as `chronon_content`, projector with chronons and card (one projector, not two); no `workstation_child` item, no second workstation
@fails `getDrops` overrides adding to the now-loaded table (`WorkstationBlock`, `AbstractMarkerBlock`, `MetronomeBlock`, `RudimentaryTempadBlock`); a tool requirement (`needs_iron_tool` tag) if bare hand drops nothing
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-TP-33
@group A
@commands #10 terminal half and explosions: place a workstation with a docked Tempad, break the terminal half in survival; place a marker (also a chronomark or projector), `summon tnt` beside it with `Fuse:1` (workstation and metronome resist 1200: TNT cannot break them, as upstream)
@pass terminal break: pad and terminal gone, one workstation and the Tempad dropped; TNT: the blocks drop their item (`survives_explosion` condition rolls), no duplicate workstation from the terminal
@fails `WorkstationChildBlock.playerWillDestroy` (destroyBlock on the pad); explosion path calls getDrops of both halves
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-TP-34
@group A
@commands #12 creative breaks: `gamemode creative qa`; place a workstation, dock a Tempad, `/ztp break qa` the pad; repeat breaking the terminal; repeat with the workstation powered (door open)
@pass both halves gone, **no item entities** (`execute if entity @e[type=item,distance=..30]` count 0), no ghost terminal (`/ztp blocks`); powered case: the door closes; latest.log has no exception
@fails `WorkstationBlock.playerWillDestroy` flags (UPDATE_KNOWN_SHAPE); a terminal left standing = the shape update was needed to clear something else
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-TP-35
@group A
@commands #12 survival unchanged: survival break of the pad and of the terminal, each with a docked Tempad and the workstation powered; then place a block in the terminal's spot and check placement still refused
@pass one workstation + the Tempad each time; open door closes; placement rule unchanged
@fails the flag change must only touch the creative branch
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-TP-36
@group A
@commands #11 anchor id across a restart: place a Timedoor Marker and a Chronomark, name them, write a card from each (blank card use on the block); `/data get block` both; `/save-all`, restart; `/data get block` again, `/ztp anchors`, `/ztp locs qa`
@pass before and after: `anchor_id` holds the UUID the card's `portal_target.id` holds, `id` is the type id; anchors file one entry per marker; both listed under markers
@fails `AbstractMarkerBe` ID = `anchor_id`, `parseUuid` on load
